Day 70/100 of hashtag#DrGViswanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 222 – Count Complete Tree Nodes 
This problem was a great exercise in using the properties of a Complete Binary Tree to do better than a simple O(n) traversal.
- Approach:
For every node, I calculate:
The height of the leftmost path
The height of the rightmost path
If both heights are equal, the subtree is a perfect binary tree, so its number of nodes can be calculated directly using:
2^h - 1
Otherwise, I recursively count the nodes in the left and right subtrees.

Time complexity : O(log² n)
Space complexity : O(log n) 

-Key Takeaways:
Complete binary trees have useful structural properties that can be exploited.
We don't always need to visit every node.
Calculating the left and right heights helps identify a perfect subtree.
Combining tree height + recursion can significantly improve efficiency.
